WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.471
"Rosie!" Mom called. "We're waiting!"

2
00:00:09.472 --> 00:00:13.601
Rosie was juggling some tennis balls.

3
00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:20.467
"Coming!" she answered.

4
00:00:20.468 --> 00:00:24.318
Rosie's brother Zack had a piano lesson today.

5
00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:29.732
After that, their brother Jimmy had a baseball game.

6
00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:32.788
"Hmm," thought Rosie.

7
00:00:32.789 --> 00:00:35.648
"It'll be a long morning.

8
00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:39.704
Maybe I can practice during the boys' activities."

9
00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:42.378
She put the balls in her backpack.

10
00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:50.230
Then she ran outside to the car.

11
00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:55.578
Zack was annoyed. "What took you so long, Rosie?"

12
00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:59.912
"I know what she was doing," Jimmy said.

13
00:00:59.913 --> 00:01:04.514
"She was practicing again."

14
00:01:04.515 --> 00:01:07.223
Zack laughed.

15
00:01:07.224 --> 00:01:10.162
"Rosie, you can't even catch one ball!

16
00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:13.270
You'll never learn how to juggle!"

17
00:01:13.271 --> 00:01:16.461
Rosie's cheeks turned pink.

18
00:01:16.462 --> 00:01:20.756
Zack was a talented piano player.

19
00:01:20.757 --> 00:01:24.475
Jimmy was the best hitter on his baseball team.

20
00:01:24.476 --> 00:01:27.606
Rosie wanted to have a talent too.

21
00:01:27.607 --> 00:01:37.731
"I just have to keep practicing," she thought.

22
00:01:37.732 --> 00:01:40.744
Later the family was having a snack.

23
00:01:40.745 --> 00:01:44.249
Suddenly they heard a boom!

24
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:50.183
"Thunder!" said Jimmy.

25
00:01:50.184 --> 00:01:54.674
Outside, rain poured down and lightning flashed.

26
00:01:54.675 --> 00:01:58.848
Inside, the lights flickered and then went out.

27
00:01:58.849 --> 00:02:10.680
Zack groaned. "We just lost our electricity."

28
00:02:10.681 --> 00:02:18.397
Mom went to call the electric company.

29
00:02:18.398 --> 00:02:23.964
"No TV." Jimmy sighed.

30
00:02:23.965 --> 00:02:27.747
"No computer," Zack grumbled.

31
00:02:27.748 --> 00:02:31.491
"This is so boring."

32
00:02:31.492 --> 00:02:35.955
Rosie reached into her backpack.

33
00:02:35.956 --> 00:02:37.911
She took a deep breath.

34
00:02:37.912 --> 00:02:44.573
She tossed one, two, three balls into the air.

35
00:02:44.574 --> 00:02:47.749
"You're juggling!" Zack cried.

36
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:54.682
Jimmy clapped. "You did it!"

37
00:02:54.683 --> 00:03:01.676
The boys watched Rosie juggle the tennis balls.

38
00:03:01.677 --> 00:03:06.088
Then she got some oranges and juggled those too.

39
00:03:06.089 --> 00:03:10.971
"Can you teach us how to juggle?" asked Zack.

40
00:03:10.972 --> 00:03:16.271
"Sure." Rosie grinned. "I finally have a talent."

41
00:03:16.272 --> 00:03:20.405
Jimmy shook his head. "You have two talents."

42
00:03:20.406 --> 00:03:22.668
"Two?" said Rosie.

43
00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.850
"Yep," said Jimmy.

44
00:03:24.851 --> 00:03:33.101
"Juggling—and working hard!"

